      "text": "To find the \\(2 \\times 2\\) matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) such that \\(\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we start by expressing \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) in its general form:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nGiven the equations:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3a \\\\ 3c \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\nwe can solve for \\(a\\) and \\(c\\):\n\\[\n3a = 6 \\implies a = 2,\n\\]\n\\[\n3c = 21 \\implies c = 7.\n\\]\n\nNext, using the second equation:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -a + 5b \\\\ -c + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(a = 2\\) and \\(c = 7\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -2 + 5b \\\\ -7 + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nThis gives us the system of equations:\n\\[\n-2 + 5b = 3 \\implies 5b = 5 \\implies b = 1,\n\\]\n\\[\n-7 + 5d = -17 \\implies 5d = -10 \\implies d = -2.\n\\]\nThus, the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]",
